1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,317
What if every volcano on Earth erupted at the same time?

2
00:00:03,817 --> 00:00:07,833
There are about 1,350 potentially active volcanoes.

3
00:00:07,833 --> 00:00:11,299
In a normal year, only forty to fifty erupt.

4
00:00:11,783 --> 00:00:13,543
Day one, the skies close.

5
00:00:13,543 --> 00:00:18,682
In 2010, one Icelandic volcano cancelled over a hundred thousand flights.

6
00:00:18,982 --> 00:00:20,932
Like and subscribe for more what-ifs.

7
00:00:21,417 --> 00:00:22,844
Then the sulfur haze.

8
00:00:22,844 --> 00:00:28,148
In 1991, Pinatubo alone cooled the Northern Hemisphere by about half a degree.

9
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:32,066
In 1815, Tambora caused a year without a summer.

10
00:00:32,066 --> 00:00:34,414
Snow fell in New England in July.

11
00:00:34,917 --> 00:00:36,712
Now imagine all of them at once.

12
00:00:37,217 --> 00:00:38,579
So could it really happen?

13
00:00:38,579 --> 00:00:39,941
Full story on the channel.
